# Backend Specification - .NET C# Integration

## Overview
This document outlines the entities, API endpoints, and business logic required to migrate the current Bookio frontend (Next.js) to a robust .NET C# backend.

## 1. Data Entities (C# Models)

### Core Identity & Users
```csharp
public class User
{
    public Guid Id { get; set; }
    public string Email { get; set; }
    public string PasswordHash { get; set; } // ASP.NET Identity
    public string FirstName { get; set; } // "Namn" split?
    public string LastName { get; set; }
    public string Phone { get; set; }
    public DateTime? DateOfBirth { get; set; }
    public UserRole Role { get; set; } // User, BusinessAdmin, SuperAdmin
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
}

public enum UserRole
{
    User,
    BusinessOwner,
    SuperAdmin
}
```

### Business Domain
```csharp
public class Business
{
    public Guid Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public string Slug { get; set; } // For SEO-friendly URLs
    public string Description { get; set; }
    public string Address { get; set; }
    public string City { get; set; }
    public string Category { get; set; } // Could be an Enum or separate Entity
    public double Rating { get; set; } // Aggregated from reviews
    public string ImageUrl { get; set; }
    
    // Relationships
    public Guid OwnerId { get; set; }
    public User Owner { get; set; }
    public ICollection<Service> Services { get; set; }
    public ICollection<Staff> Staff { get; set; }
    public ICollection<Review> Reviews { get; set; }
}

public class BusinessSettings 
{
    public Guid BusinessId { get; set; }
    public string Currency { get; set; } = "SEK";
    public string TimeZone { get; set; } = "Europe/Stockholm";
    // Booking rules, cancellation policies etc.
}
```

### Service & Resources
```csharp
public class Service
{
    public Guid Id { get; set; }
    public Guid BusinessId { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } // e.g., "Herrklippning"
    public string Description { get; set; }
    public int DurationMinutes { get; set; }
    public decimal Price { get; set; }
    public bool IsActive { get; set; }
}

public class Staff
{
    public Guid Id { get; set; }
    public Guid BusinessId { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public string Title { get; set; } // e.g., "Frisör", "Terapeut"
    public string ImageUrl { get; set; }
    public string Bio { get; set; }
    public bool IsActive { get; set; }
    
    // Which services can this staff perform?
    public ICollection<Service> QualifiedServices { get; set; }
}

public class Schedule // Working hours
{
    public Guid Id { get; set; }
    public Guid StaffId { get; set; } // Or BusinessId if generic
    public DayOfWeek DayOfWeek { get; set; }
    public TimeSpan StartTime { get; set; }
    public TimeSpan EndTime { get; set; }
    public bool IsDayOff { get; set; }
}
```

### Booking Domain
```csharp
public class Booking
{
    public Guid Id { get; set; }
    public string BookingReference { get; set; } // Friendly ID e.g., "BK-12345"
    
    public Guid BusinessId { get; set; }
    public Guid ServiceId { get; set; }
    public Guid? StaffId { get; set; } // Optional if "Any staff" selected
    
    // Customer Info (Linked to User if logged in, otherwise guest details)
    public Guid? CustomerId { get; set; }
    public string CustomerName { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; }
    public string CustomerPhone { get; set; }
    
    public DateTime StartTime { get; set; }
    public DateTime EndTime { get; set; } // Calculated from Duration
    
    public BookingStatus Status { get; set; }
    
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
}

public enum BookingStatus
{
    Pending,
    Confirmed,
    Cancelled,
    Completed,
    NoShow
}

public class Review
{
    public Guid Id { get; set; }
    public Guid BusinessId { get; set; }
    public Guid UserId { get; set; }
    public int Rating { get; set; } // 1-5
    public string Comment { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
}
```

## 2. API Endpoints

### Authentication (Identity)
- `POST /api/auth/register` - Create new user account
- `POST /api/auth/login` - Authenticate and get Token (JWT)
- `POST /api/auth/refresh-token`
- `POST /api/auth/forgot-password`
- `GET /api/auth/me` - Get current user profile

### Business (Public)
- `GET /api/businesses` - Search/List businesses (filters: city, category, query)
- `GET /api/businesses/{slug}` - Get details for a specific business
- `GET /api/businesses/{slug}/services` - List services for business
- `GET /api/businesses/{slug}/reviews` - List reviews

### Booking (Public/User)
- `GET /api/businesses/{id}/availability?date=...&serviceId=...` - Get available slots
  - **Logic**: Check Staff schedules, subtract existing bookings, ensure Service duration fits.
- `POST /api/bookings` - Create a new booking
  - **Logic**: Validate availability again (race condition check), send confirmation email.
- `GET /api/user/bookings` - List my bookings
- `POST /api/bookings/{id}/cancel` - Cancel booking (check cancellation policy)

### Business Administration (Protected - Owner/Admin)
- `GET /api/admin/dashboard/stats` - Stats (Revenue, bookings, activity)
- `GET /api/admin/bookings` - List all bookings for business
- `PUT /api/admin/bookings/{id}/status` - Update status (e.g. mark as NoShow)
- `POST /api/admin/services` - Create service
- `PUT /api/admin/services/{id}` - Update service
- `POST /api/admin/staff` - Add staff member
- `PUT /api/admin/staff/{id}/schedule` - Update working hours
- `GET /api/admin/settings` - Get business settings

### Application Administration (Super Admin)
- `GET /api/superadmin/businesses` - List all businesses
- `PUT /api/superadmin/businesses/{id}/status` - Approve/Suspend business

## 3. Important Logic & Considerations

1.  **Availability Calculation**:
    *   This is the most complex logic.
    *   Must intersect **Staff Working Hours** with **Service Duration**.
    *   Must subtract **Existing Bookings**.
    *   *Edge Case*: "Any Staff" selection needs to aggregate all qualified staff availability.

2.  **Time Zones**:
    *   backend should store everything in UTC.
    *   APIs should separate "Slot Time" (Utc) from "Business Local Time" context if needed, but standardizing on returning ISO8601 strings is best.

3.  **Concurrency**:
    *   Two users booking the same slot at the same time. Use database transactions or optimistic concurrency checks (`RowVersion`) when creating a booking.

4.  **Guest vs Registered Bookings**:
    *   Allow creating bookings without a `UserId`, but capture `CustomerEmail` and `CustomerPhone`.
    *   Verify email format strictly.

5.  **Notifications**:
    *   Trigger Email/SMS on `BookingCreated`, `BookingCancelled`, `BookingReminder`.
    *   Use a background job (e.g., Hangfire) for Reminders.
